\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. At the Cross, her station keeping,
\par Stood the mournful mother weeping,
\par Where He hung, the dying Lord;
\par For her soul, of joy bereaved,
\par Bowed with anguish, deeply grieved,
\par Felt the sharp and piercing sword.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. O how sad and sore distressed
\par Now was she, that mother blessed
\par Of the sole-begotten One;
\par Deep the woe of her affliction,
\par When she saw the crucifixion,
\par Of her evr-glorious Son.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. For His people's sins chastised,
\par She beheld her Son despised,
\par Scourged, and crowned with thorns entwined;
\par Saw Him the from judgement taken,
\par And in death by all forsaken
\par Till His spirit He resigned.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Jesus, may her deep devotion
\par Stir in me the same emotion,
\par Fount of love, Redeemer kind,
\par That my heart, fresh ardour gaining,
\par And a purer love attaining,
\par May with Thee acceptance find.
\par                                      Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

